IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulation 22.01 and its Schedule (the social security
-- agreements whose treatment of spouses is extended to common-law partners) and regulation 22.1 (the events in relation to a
-- sponsor, and the sponsors to whom they apply).
--
-- The Schedule is data, not logic: it is a list of the 44 rows of the printed table, generated from the source text by script and
-- compared with it by the srcrefs gate. A country is looked up by its name exactly as the Schedule prints it ("Austria (Republic of)",
-- "United States of America"). The agreement column is kept as printed: a row that lists several instruments keeps them in one
-- string, because the source text runs them together without a separator.

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Application of International Agreements`

-- src:244 | 22.01 The agreements referred to in the schedule, which were entered into under subsection 40(1) of the Act for the making of reciprocal arrangements relating to the administration or operation of the Act, shall, in order to give full effect to the Act, be applied in Canada in a manner that extends to common-law partners the treatment afforded to spouses.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22.01 (src:244)
GIVEN `the country named in the agreement` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22.01: the agreement with the country is one referred to in the Schedule` `the country named in the agreement` MEANS
    count (filter `an entry for the country` `reg 22.01: the Schedule`) GREATER THAN 0
    WHERE
        `an entry for the country` entry MEANS
            entry's `Country` EQUALS `the country named in the agreement`

-- 22.01 says what the agreements are applied to do: extend to common-law partners the treatment afforded to spouses. The one fact
-- that decides whether a person gets that treatment is whether the agreement is one of those in the Schedule.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22.01 (src:244)
GIVEN `the country named in the agreement` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22.01: the treatment afforded to spouses is extended to common-law partners under the agreement with the country` `the country named in the agreement` MEANS
    `reg 22.01: the agreement with the country is one referred to in the Schedule` `the country named in the agreement`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22.01 (src:244)
GIVEN `the country named in the agreement` IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 22.01: the agreements of the Schedule with the country, as printed` `the country named in the agreement` MEANS
    map `the agreement of an entry` (filter `an entry for the country` `reg 22.01: the Schedule`)
    WHERE
        `an entry for the country` entry MEANS
            entry's `Country` EQUALS `the country named in the agreement`
        `the agreement of an entry` entry MEANS
            entry's `Agreement`

§§ `Sponsorship Immigrants`

-- 22.1(1): for sections 11(8), 19(6.2) and 21(9.1) of the Act, four things count as events in relation to a sponsor: (a) the sponsor's
-- death, (b) conviction of a Criminal Code offence relating to the sponsored individual, (c) a determination that the sponsor is a
-- bankrupt, (d) sentencing to a term of imprisonment of more than six months. The term is a number of months (a fraction of a month is
-- allowed); NOTHING means the sponsor has not been sentenced.
-- src:247 | 22.1 (1) For the purposes of subsections 11(8), 19(6.2) and 21(9.1) of the Act, the following are events in relation to a sponsor referred to in those subsections:
-- src:248 | (a) the death of the sponsor;
-- src:249 | (b) the sponsor’s conviction of an offence under the Criminal Code relating to the sponsored individual;
-- src:250 | (c) a determination that the sponsor is a bankrupt as defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act; and
-- src:251 | (d) the sentencing of the sponsor to a term of imprisonment of more than six months.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22.1(1) (src:247-251)
DECLARE `reg 22.1(1): Event in relation to a sponsor` IS ONE OF
    `reg 22.1(1)(a): the death of the sponsor`
    `reg 22.1(1)(b): the sponsor's conviction of an offence under the Criminal Code relating to the sponsored individual`
    `reg 22.1(1)(c): a determination that the sponsor is a bankrupt as defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act`
    `reg 22.1(1)(d): the sentencing of the sponsor to a term of imprisonment of more than six months`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22.1(1) (src:247-251)
GIVEN `the sponsor has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sponsor has been convicted of an offence under the Criminal Code relating to the sponsored individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been determined that the sponsor is a bankrupt as defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment, in months, to which the sponsor has been sentenced` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 22.1(1): Event in relation to a sponsor`
`reg 22.1(1): the events that have occurred in relation to the sponsor` `the sponsor has died` `the sponsor has been convicted of an offence under the Criminal Code relating to the sponsored individual` `it has been determined that the sponsor is a bankrupt as defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` `the term of imprisonment, in months, to which the sponsor has been sentenced` MEANS
    append `the event of paragraph (a)` (append `the event of paragraph (b)` (append `the event of paragraph (c)` `the event of paragraph (d)`))
    WHERE
        `the event of paragraph (a)` MEANS
            IF `the sponsor has died` THEN LIST `reg 22.1(1)(a): the death of the sponsor` ELSE EMPTY
        `the event of paragraph (b)` MEANS
            IF `the sponsor has been convicted of an offence under the Criminal Code relating to the sponsored individual` THEN LIST `reg 22.1(1)(b): the sponsor's conviction of an offence under the Criminal Code relating to the sponsored individual` ELSE EMPTY
        `the event of paragraph (c)` MEANS
            IF `it has been determined that the sponsor is a bankrupt as defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` THEN LIST `reg 22.1(1)(c): a determination that the sponsor is a bankrupt as defined in section 2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` ELSE EMPTY
        `the event of paragraph (d)` MEANS
            IF `the sentence is of more than six months` THEN LIST `reg 22.1(1)(d): the sentencing of the sponsor to a term of imprisonment of more than six months` ELSE EMPTY
        `the sentence is of more than six months` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the term of imprisonment, in months, to which the sponsor has been sentenced`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST months THEN months GREATER THAN 6

-- 22.1(2): subsection (1) applies to a sponsor (a) whose undertaking was in effect on or after March 7, 1996, and (b) to whom an event
-- of (1)(a) to (d) occurred on or after March 7, 1996. An undertaking was in effect on or after that day unless it ended before it,
-- so the input is the last day it was in effect (NOTHING: it still is).
-- src:252 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a sponsor
-- src:253 | (a) whose undertaking in respect of a pensioner, the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner, or a survivor, as the case may be, was in effect on or after March 7, 1996; and
-- src:254 | (b) to whom an event referred to in any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (d) occurred on or after March 7, 1996.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 22.1(2) (src:252-254)
GIVEN `the last day on which the sponsor's undertaking in respect of the pensioner, the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner, or the survivor was in effect` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the days on which the events referred to in any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (d) occurred` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22.1(2): subsection (1) applies to the sponsor` `the last day on which the sponsor's undertaking in respect of the pensioner, the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner, or the survivor was in effect` `the days on which the events referred to in any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (d) occurred` MEANS
        `the undertaking was in effect on or after March 7, 1996`
    AND `an event occurred on or after March 7, 1996`
    WHERE
        `the day that is March 7, 1996` MEANS
            YearMonthDay 1996 3 7
        `the undertaking was in effect on or after March 7, 1996` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day on which the sponsor's undertaking in respect of the pensioner, the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner, or the survivor was in effect`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST last THEN last AT LEAST `the day that is March 7, 1996`
        `an event on or after March 7, 1996` day MEANS
            day AT LEAST `the day that is March 7, 1996`
        `an event occurred on or after March 7, 1996` MEANS
            count (filter `an event on or after March 7, 1996` `the days on which the events referred to in any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (d) occurred`) GREATER THAN 0

